  "body": "Found in the review of PR #3532. The fault was on `main` before that PR (the crate `camcraft-gpu`, PR #3363).\n\n## What happens\nEach GPU call of the crate runs in an error scope. The crate does not install a handler for an uncaptured error, and none for a lost device, on the shared device. An error outside a scope (for example a device that is lost when the driver restarts) goes to the default handler of wgpu. The default handler panics.\n\nAGENTS.md: \"No panic in a system or on a path that a user can start.\"\n\n## Wanted\n- Install the two handlers when the shared device is made. A handler turns the GPU path off, logs the reason one time, and the callers get the CPU result.\n- A test proves that a call after a simulated device loss gives the CPU result and no panic.\n",
